    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224-a3">

                <pb facs="0406" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg366"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to the
                        Chancellor of Oxford</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 8, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> On behalf of my country, I receive with
                    the most profound sensibility the intelligence which, as chancellor of the
                    University of Oxford, you communicate respecting the extraordinary action it has
                    taken in regard to the late afflicting event in America.</p>
                <p>That the high standard of education established in that University should excite
                    a strong abhorrence of the act of the assassin, in the present case, is no more
                    than could be naturally expected; but that the authorities should resort to an
                    unusal method of expressing their sense of it, and at the same time couple with
                    it the most friendly wishes for the restoration of peace and prosperity to
                    America, is a circumstance which cannot fail to be fully appreciated, as well as
                    to stimulate good will among the people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl of Derby,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
